  "explanation": {
    "event_selection": "The unified specification uses only task-level delivery actions, color observations, pickup and delivery outcomes, and claim coordination events needed to select one available box and deliver it to the matching zone. Low-level movement, obstacle, unrelated release reception, and remote delivery reception events are omitted because collision_avoidance already protects motion and those events do not define the local delivery sequence.",
    "transition_design": "searching_objects repeatedly enables search_object and branches on the observed box color. Each claim-attempt state enables only the matching claim event and abandons the attempt on the matching received_claim event or loss of visibility. A successful claim immediately enters an approach state where approach_object repeats; loss of visibility returns to claimed search, and reaching the object from either claimed search or approach enables pick_up_object. Pickup failure releases the matching claim, while pickup confirmation starts matching-zone search. search_zone and approach_zone repeat in their respective phases, not-visible observations return to zone search, and drop_object is enabled only after the matching zone is reached. Delivery failure restarts matching-zone search, while confirmation requires the matching publish_delivered event before delivery_complete. Cross-color pickup, zone, drop, and publication sequences are excluded.",
    "feedback_response": "No previous-run feedback was supplied."
